I have found that the most frustrating things about nethack are the traps. I
think that it is a good idea to have them, but to not be able to disarm them
is quite frustrating. The only ones that I have been able to overcome are
pits and trap doors. (I will not say how because if a person doesn't know, 
I think that figuring out how is harmless enough).

What I propose is to allow the player to disarm the trap, but have a chance
to fail that is based on int., wis., dex, and class (i.e. rogue vs. barbarian).
upon successful disarming, the trap will dissappear. If the character fails,
then either nothing happens, the trap is activated once, or in the case of 
magic traps, all possible events that the magic trap can cause occur. Failure
to disarm a rust trap can cause all non-rustproof items that the character
has to take -1 damage (including unwielded items).

Also, have a spellbook/wand/scroll of detect trap and of disarm trap that the
player may use. To balance the scroll/wand, create a wand/scroll of create
trap that will create traps on the eight adjacent squares and the space that
the player is standing upon.

Conversly, the player should be able to set certain traps in strategic
locations. If the player screws up the setting of the trap, it goes off!


